      "template": "<div lang=\"en\" style=\"width:100%; min-height:100vh; background:#0a0a09; font-family:'Cormorant Garamond', serif; box-sizing:border-box;\">\n\n  \n\n  \n\n  <main data-pagefind-meta=\"url:/en/collection/spanish-colonial-coinage/2-escudos-felipe-v-bogota/\" id=\"main-content\" tabindex=\"-1\" style=\"max-width:1180px; margin:0 auto; padding:56px 24px 80px; outline:none;\">\n\n    <a href=\"/en/collection/spanish-colonial-coinage/\" style=\"display:inline-block; color:#e7ddc4; text-decoration:none; font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.08em; margin-bottom:24px;\">&larr; Spanish colonial coin catalog</a>\n\n    <div style=\"background:#d8d2cd; border:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.08); border-radius:3px; padding:clamp(28px,4vw,64px); box-shadow:0 30px 70px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);\">\n\n      <div style=\"text-align:center; max-width:760px; margin:0 auto 48px;\">\n        <span style=\"display:block; font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.22em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; margin-bottom:14px;\">Spanish Colonial Currency &middot; Viceroyalty of New Granada &middot; Reign of Philip V (1700&ndash;1746)</span>\n        <h1 style=\"font-family:'Montenegrin Gothic One', serif; font-weight:400; font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,46px); line-height:1.08; letter-spacing:0.01em; color:#1c1a15; margin:0 0 12px;\">2 Shield Gold Doubloon</h1>\n        <p style=\"font-size:clamp(19px,2vw,23px); font-style:italic; color:#4a4331; margin:0;\">Macuquina &middot; Mint of Santa Fe de Bogotá</p>\n      </div>\n<div style=\"width:100%; max-width:760px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px; margin:0 auto 40px;\">\n<button\n            data-zoom-trigger=\"doblon-2-escudos\"\n            aria-label=\"Enlarge image of the doblón de 2 escudos\"\n            style=\"all:unset; display:block; width:100%; position:relative; cursor:zoom-in; background:#1c1a15; border-radius:4px; padding:24px;\"\n          >\n            <picture>\n              <source srcset=\"/uploads/colombia-2-escudos-felipe-v-santa-fe-bogota.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n              <img\n                src=\"/uploads/colombia-2-escudos-felipe-v-santa-fe-bogota.jpg\"\n                alt=\"Gold 2-escudo doubloon of Philip V, Santa Fe de Bogotá mint — obverse with a Jerusalem cross (left) and reverse with the Pillars of Hercules (right)\"\n                width=\"564\"\n                height=\"277\"\n                loading=\"eager\"\n                decoding=\"async\"\n                style=\"display:block; width:100%; height:auto;\"\n              />\n            </picture>\n            <span style=\"position:absolute; bottom:22px; right:22px; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; background:rgba(10,10,9,0.82); color:#d8d2cd; font-size:13px; letter-spacing:0.08em; padding:8px 14px; border-radius:999px;\">\n              <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; background:#d8d2cd; transform:rotate(45deg);\"></span>Enlarge</span>\n          </button>\n          <span style=\"font-size:13px; letter-spacing:0.08em; color:#5c4e33; text-align:center; font-style:italic;\">Obverse (left) and reverse (right) — Notofilia.com Collection</span>\n</div>\n\n      <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.75; color:#332e22; max-width:760px; margin:0 auto 56px;\">Hand-struck at the Santa Fe de Bogotá mint &mdash;one of the Spanish Empire’s main gold-producing centers in the New World&mdash;, this 2-escudo cob represents trade gold coinage in its most artisanal form. Gold bars were melted, hand-cut into irregular planchets, and struck with hammer dies, an entirely manual process that made each piece unique.</p>\n\n      <section id=\"doblon-2-escudos\" style=\"max-width:760px; margin:0 auto;\">\n\n        <div style=\"display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px; margin:0 0 40px;\">\n          \n<div style=\"display:flex; flex-direction:column;\">\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Country / Viceroyalty</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">New Granada (present-day Colombia)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Mint</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Santa Fe de Bogotá (&ldquo;SF&rdquo; mintmark)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Reign</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Philip V, first Bourbon king of Spain (1700&ndash;1746)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Denomination</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">2 gold escudos (&ldquo;doubloon&rdquo;)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Composition</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Gold .917 (22 carats)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Gross weight</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">~6.76 g (typical range in macuquinas: 6.65&ndash;6.82 g)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Fine gold content</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">0.1995 troy oz (~6.2 g pure gold)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Diameter</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">~20&ndash;24 mm (irregular cospel typical of the macuquina)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Manufacturing Method</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Hand minting on cut cospel (macuquina)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12); border-bottom:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n            <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Catalog references</span>\n            <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">KM #17.2 &middot; Restrepo M80 &middot; Calico Type 243 &middot; Friedberg Fr-8<span style=\"display:block; font-size:15px; font-style:italic; color:#5c4e33; margin-top:4px;\">(general type 1714&ndash;1743; the exact subtype depends on the year and assayer)</span></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n\n          \n            <div\n              role=\"dialog\"\n              aria-modal=\"true\"\n              aria-label=\"Enlarged Doblón de 2 escudos\"\n              data-zoom-dialog=\"doblon-2-escudos\" hidden\n             \n             class=\"catalog-zoom-dialog\">\n              <button\n                data-zoom-close\n                aria-label=\"Close\"\n                style=\"position:absolute; top:24px; right:28px; background:transparent; border:1px solid rgba(231,222,201,0.4); color:#d8d2cd; font-size:22px; line-height:1; width:44px; height:44px; border-radius:50%; cursor:pointer;\"\n              >&times;</button>\n\n              <div style=\"position:absolute; top:24px; left:28px; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:6px; background:rgba(10,10,9,0.5); border:1px solid rgba(231,222,201,0.25); border-radius:999px; padding:6px;\">\n                <button disabled=\"true\" aria-label=\"Zoom out\" style=\"width:38px; height:38px; border-radius:50%; border:none; background:transparent; color:#d8d2cd; font-size:20px; cursor:pointer;\">&minus;</button>\n                <span style=\"min-width:56px; text-align:center; font-size:14px; color:#e7ddc4; letter-spacing:0.05em;\">100%</span>\n                <button disabled=\"false\" aria-label=\"Zoom in\" style=\"width:38px; height:38px; border-radius:50%; border:none; background:transparent; color:#d8d2cd; font-size:20px; cursor:pointer;\">&#43;</button>\n              </div>\n\n              <div\n                style=\"overflow:hidden; max-width:92vw; max-height:74vh; touch-action:none;\"\n              >\n                <picture>\n                  <source srcset=\"/uploads/colombia-2-escudos-felipe-v-santa-fe-bogota.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n                  <img\n                    src=\"/uploads/colombia-2-escudos-felipe-v-santa-fe-bogota.jpg\"\n                    alt=\"Doblón de oro de 2 escudos de Felipe V, enlarged view\"\n                    draggable=\"false\"\n                    style=\"display:block; max-width:92vw; max-height:74vh; width:auto; height:auto; transform:; cursor:zoom-in; user-select:none;\"\n                  />\n                </picture>\n              </div>\n\n              <span style=\"margin-top:18px; font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.06em; color:#b7ab8a; font-style:italic;\">Drag to move &middot; Mouse wheel to zoom</span>\n            </div>\n          \n        </div>\n\n        \n\n        <section style=\"margin-top:44px;\">\n          <h3 style=\"font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 14px; font-style:normal;\">Obverse and Reverse</h3>\n          <ul style=\"list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px;\">\n            <li style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:baseline;\">\n              <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; min-width:6px; background:#5c4e33; transform:rotate(45deg); position:relative; top:-3px;\"></span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.6; color:#332e22;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Obverse &mdash; The Cross:</strong>large cross of Jerusalem minted by hand, with arms ending in a potentized cross, framed in a four-leaf border. Alternating in the quadrants of the cross appear two stylized castles (Castilla) and two lions (León).</span>\n            </li>\n            <li style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:baseline;\">\n              <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; min-width:6px; background:#5c4e33; transform:rotate(45deg); position:relative; top:-3px;\"></span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.6; color:#332e22;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Reverse &mdash; Columns and Waves:</strong>the Pillars of Hercules standing on stylized waves, a symbol of Spanish expansion across the Atlantic. In the central grid appears the denomination &ldquo;2&rdquo;, flanked by the mint mark &ldquo;SF&rdquo; (Santa Fe de Bogotá) and the assayer's mark; The lower register bears the date, when visible on the blank.</span>\n            </li>\n          </ul>\n        </section>\n\n      </section>\n\n      <blockquote style=\"max-width:760px; margin:56px auto 0; padding:28px 0 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.15);\">\n        <p style=\"font-size:20px; font-style:italic; line-height:1.7; color:#4a4331; margin:0 0 10px;\">Minted in Santa Fe de Bogotá, this macuquina belongs to the first stage of a mint founded in 1622, where the first gold coins made in America were produced. Under the reign of Philip V, bars of gold were melted, cut by hand into blanks, and struck with dice on an anvil. The irregular shape of each piece testifies to this process prior to mechanization with flywheel presses, implemented in Santa Fe since 1757.</p>\n        <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.08em; color:#5c4e33;\">&mdash; Historical Context Note</span>\n      </blockquote>\n\n      <section style=\"max-width:760px; margin:32px auto 0; padding-top:24px; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n        <h2 style=\"font-size:13px; letter-spacing:0.18em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 12px; font-style:normal;\">Sources</h2>\n        <ul style=\"margin:0; padding:0 0 0 20px; font-size:15px; line-height:1.7; color:#5c4e33; font-style:italic;\">\n          <li>Restrepo Restrepo, José Ignacio.<em>Two Hundred Years of Republican Currency in Colombia (1810–2010)</em>— base reference for the Restrepo number.</li>\n          <li>Calicó, Ferrán, Xavier and Adolfo.<em>Ounces, Doubloons and Shields: Hispano-American Numismatics.</em></li>\n          <li>Krause, Chester L. y Clifford Mishler.<em>Standard Catalog of World Coins.</em></li>\n          <li>Numista —<a href=\"https://en.numista.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color:#6b521f;\">numista.com<span style=\"font-style:italic; font-weight:400;\">(opens in a new tab)</span></a></li>\n          <li>Rodríguez Soage, José David.<a href=\"https://www.enumismatic.com/mints-history/santa-fe/es/la-ceca-de-santa-fe\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color:#6b521f;\">&laquo;The Santa Fe Mint&raquo;<span style=\"font-style:italic; font-weight:400;\">(opens in a new tab)</span></a>, eNumismatic, 2021.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </section>\n\n    </div>\n  </main>\n\n  \n\n</div>",
      "recordTitle": "2 Shield Gold Doubloon",
      "eyebrow": "Moneda Colonial Española · Virreinato de la Nueva Granada · Reinado de Felipe V (1700&ndash;1746)"
